    {
      "id": "harness",
      "type": "flow",
      "duration_s": 14,
      "narration": [
        "Their fix is a harness with two roles.",
        "In the first session, an initializer agent turns the prompt into a feature list: over 200 end-to-end features, all marked failing.",
        "It's JSON on purpose: the model is less likely to rewrite JSON than Markdown.",
        "It also writes a progress log, an init script that starts the dev server, and a first git commit.",
        "Every later session runs a coding agent. It reads the progress log and git history, then picks one failing feature.",
        "It starts the app, checks nothing is already broken, and builds just that one feature.",
        "Then it tests like a user would, in the browser, and only then marks the feature passing.",
        "It ends by committing and updating the log, so the next session starts clean."
      ],
      "data": {
        "roles": {
          "input": "neutral",
          "agent": "c2",
          "artifact": "c1",
          "step": "c4"
        },
        "panels": [
